/-!
# The free rigid monoidal category on a duality signature

A *duality signature* consists of a type of generating objects and a type of generating
morphisms (*coupons*), each coupon having a source and a target which are formal rigid objects
(`TauCeti.RigidObject`): expressions built from the generators by tensor products, the unit and
formal right and left duals. A coupon `A ⊗ Bᘁ ⟶ C` thus keeps its two input ports, the second of
which is a dual port, and a coupon may have the unit as source or target. Tensor signatures are
the special case in which no boundary mentions a dual, embedding via
`TauCeti.TensorSignature.toDualitySignature`.

The free rigid monoidal category `DualitySignature.FreeRigid S` on a signature `S` has the formal
rigid objects as objects. Its morphisms are formal composites, tensor products and whiskerings of
identities, associators, unitors, coupons, and evaluations and coevaluations for the formal right
dual `Xᘁ` and the formal left dual `ᘁX` of every object `X`, modulo exactly the axioms of a
monoidal category and the zigzag identities of the two exact pairings `(X, Xᘁ)` and `(ᘁX, X)`.
No equation between coupons is imposed, and duals of different handedness or iterated duals of
the same handedness are never identified: `Xᘁᘁ` and `X` are distinct objects
(`FreeRigid.of_ne_doubleRightDual`), and no pivotal structure is installed.

## Main definitions and results

* `TauCeti.DualitySignature` and `TauCeti.TensorSignature.toDualitySignature`: generating objects
  and coupons with formal rigid boundaries, together with the inclusion from tensor signatures.
* `TauCeti.DualitySignature.FreeRigid S`: the free rigid monoidal category on `S`, constructed via
  the shared presentation core `TauCeti.MonoidalCore`, with `FreeRigid.of` and
  `FreeRigid.coupon` for the generators, and its `RigidCategory` instance whose chosen duals are
  the formal ones.
* `FreeRigid.Hom.inductionOn`: morphisms are generated by identities, structural isomorphisms,
  evaluations, coevaluations and coupons under composition and whiskering.
* `FreeRigid.lift fo fc`: the strong monoidal functor into an arbitrary (not necessarily strict)
  rigid monoidal category determined by images `fo` of the generating objects and `fc` of the
  coupons. It interprets objects by `RigidObject.eval`, so it sends the chosen duals of
  `S.FreeRigid` to the chosen duals of the target (`FreeRigid.lift_mapRightDualIso`,
  `FreeRigid.lift_mapLeftDualIso`), and the formal evaluations and coevaluations to those of the
  target (`FreeRigid.lift_map_evaluation_rightDual`, `FreeRigid.lift_map_coevaluation_rightDual`,
  `FreeRigid.lift_map_evaluation_leftDual`, `FreeRigid.lift_map_coevaluation_leftDual`).
* `FreeRigid.couponCount`, `FreeRigid.coupon_ne_id`, and `FreeRigid.coupon_ne_coupon`: coupon
  multiplicity is invariant under the rigid-category axioms, so no coupon collapses to an identity
  and distinct coupons with matching boundaries remain distinct.
* `FreeRigid.monoidalNatIso`: two strong monoidal functors into an arbitrary monoidal category that
  agree up to isomorphism on the generating objects, compatibly with the coupons, are isomorphic
  by a monoidal natural isomorphism extending the given isomorphisms. At a dual, its component is
  the mate of the inverse of the component at the object.
* `FreeRigid.natTrans_ext`: monoidal natural transformations between strong monoidal functors out
  of `S.FreeRigid` are determined by their components at the generating objects.
* `FreeRigid.wordIso_app`: a monoidal natural isomorphism between such functors is the
  isomorphism `FreeRigid.wordIso` induced by its components at the generating objects.
* `FreeRigid.mapWordIso F X`: the comparison between the image of a formal rigid object `X` under a
  strong monoidal functor `F` into a rigid monoidal category and the evaluation of `X` at the
  images of the generating objects; at a dual it is built from `F.mapRightDualIso` or
  `F.mapLeftDualIso`, and it is the identity for `FreeRigid.lift` (`FreeRigid.mapWordIso_lift`).
* `FreeRigid.wordIso_eq_mapWordIso`: the isomorphisms `FreeRigid.wordIso` are the comparisons
  `FreeRigid.mapWordIso` composed with the extension `RigidObject.evalIso` of the given
  isomorphisms to formal rigid objects. These comparisons give the groupoid form of the universal
  property in `TauCeti.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Free.DualitySignature.Interpretation`.
* `TauCeti.TensorSignature.ofFreeMonoidal`: the canonical strong monoidal functor from
  `S.FreeMonoidal` into `S.toDualitySignature.FreeRigid`.

The formal-morphism syntax and the monoidal instance factor through `TauCeti.MonoidalCore`,
adapted from Mathlib's `Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Free/Basic.lean` (Markus Himmel), with
constructors and zigzag relations added for the evaluations and coevaluations of Mathlib's
`ExactPairing`.

## References

* A. Joyal and R. Street, *Planar diagrams and tensor algebra*, unpublished manuscript (1988),
  §2 (autonomous tensor schemes and the free autonomous category).
* P. Selinger, *A survey of graphical languages for monoidal categories*, New Structures for
  Physics, Lecture Notes in Phys. 813 (2011), §4.1.
-/

public section

universe u v u' v'

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory

namespace TauCeti

/-- A duality signature: a type `Obj` of generating objects and a type `Coupon` of generating
morphisms, each coupon having a source and a target formal rigid object in the generating
objects. The boundaries may contain formal right and left duals, and may be the unit, so coupons
may have no inputs or no outputs. -/
structure DualitySignature where
  /-- The generating objects. -/
  Obj : Type u
  /-- The generating morphisms (coupons). -/
  Coupon : Type v
  /-- The source of a coupon. -/
  src : Coupon → RigidObject Obj
  /-- The target of a coupon. -/
  tgt : Coupon → RigidObject Obj

/-- Include a tensor signature as a duality signature by embedding its monoidal word boundaries
into `RigidObject`. Exposed so that `S.toDualitySignature.Obj` and `S.toDualitySignature.Coupon`
are definitionally `S.Obj` and `S.Coupon`. -/
@[expose] def TensorSignature.toDualitySignature (S : TensorSignature.{u, v}) :
    DualitySignature.{u, v} where
  Obj := S.Obj
  Coupon := S.Coupon
  src g := (S.src g).toRigidObject
  tgt g := (S.tgt g).toRigidObject

@[simp]
theorem TensorSignature.toDualitySignature_obj (S : TensorSignature.{u, v}) :
    S.toDualitySignature.Obj = S.Obj := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem TensorSignature.toDualitySignature_coupon (S : TensorSignature.{u, v}) :
    S.toDualitySignature.Coupon = S.Coupon := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem TensorSignature.toDualitySignature_src (S : TensorSignature.{u, v}) (g : S.Coupon) :
    S.toDualitySignature.src g = (S.src g).toRigidObject := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem TensorSignature.toDualitySignature_tgt (S : TensorSignature.{u, v}) (g : S.Coupon) :
    S.toDualitySignature.tgt g = (S.tgt g).toRigidObject := by rfl

namespace DualitySignature

variable (S : DualitySignature.{u, v})

open RigidObject in
/-- Extra morphism generators of `S.FreeRigid`: chosen right and left evaluations and
coevaluations together with a generator for each coupon of `S`. -/
inductive FreeRigidGen : RigidObject S.Obj → RigidObject S.Obj → Type (max u v)
  /-- The evaluation `Xᘁ ⊗ X ⟶ 𝟙` of the formal right dual. -/
  | ε_right (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : FreeRigidGen (X.rightDual.tensor X) unit
  /-- The coevaluation `𝟙 ⟶ X ⊗ Xᘁ` of the formal right dual. -/
  | η_right (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : FreeRigidGen unit (X.tensor X.rightDual)
  /-- The evaluation `X ⊗ ᘁX ⟶ 𝟙` of the formal left dual. -/
  | ε_left (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : FreeRigidGen (X.tensor X.leftDual) unit
  /-- The coevaluation `𝟙 ⟶ ᘁX ⊗ X` of the formal left dual. -/
  | η_left (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : FreeRigidGen unit (X.leftDual.tensor X)
  /-- A coupon of `S`. -/
  | coupon (g : S.Coupon) : FreeRigidGen (S.src g) (S.tgt g)

/-- The extra relations on formal rigid morphisms generated by the four zigzag identities of a
rigid monoidal category. -/
inductive FreeRigidRel :
    ∀ {X Y : RigidObject S.Obj},
      MonoidalCore.Hom RigidObject.unit RigidObject.tensor (FreeRigidGen S) X Y →
      MonoidalCore.Hom RigidObject.unit RigidObject.tensor (FreeRigidGen S) X Y → Prop
  | right_coevaluation_evaluation {X} :
      FreeRigidRel
        (((MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.η_right X)).whiskerLeft X.rightDual).comp
          ((MonoidalCore.Hom.α_inv X.rightDual X X.rightDual).comp
            ((MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.ε_right X)).whiskerRight X.rightDual)))
        ((MonoidalCore.Hom.ρ_hom X.rightDual).comp (MonoidalCore.Hom.l_inv X.rightDual))
  | right_evaluation_coevaluation {X} :
      FreeRigidRel
        (((MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.η_right X)).whiskerRight X).comp
          ((MonoidalCore.Hom.α_hom X X.rightDual X).comp
            ((MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.ε_right X)).whiskerLeft X)))
        ((MonoidalCore.Hom.l_hom X).comp (MonoidalCore.Hom.ρ_inv X))
  | left_coevaluation_evaluation {X} :
      FreeRigidRel
        (((MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.η_left X)).whiskerLeft X).comp
          ((MonoidalCore.Hom.α_inv X X.leftDual X).comp
            ((MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.ε_left X)).whiskerRight X)))
        ((MonoidalCore.Hom.ρ_hom X).comp (MonoidalCore.Hom.l_inv X))
  | left_evaluation_coevaluation {X} :
      FreeRigidRel
        (((MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.η_left X)).whiskerRight X.leftDual).comp
          ((MonoidalCore.Hom.α_hom X.leftDual X X.leftDual).comp
            ((MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.ε_left X)).whiskerLeft X.leftDual)))
        ((MonoidalCore.Hom.l_hom X.leftDual).comp (MonoidalCore.Hom.ρ_inv X.leftDual))

/-- The monoidal presentation of the free rigid monoidal category on a duality signature `S`:
formal rigid objects `RigidObject S.Obj`, duality and coupon generators `FreeRigidGen S`, and
zigzag relations `FreeRigidRel S`. -/
@[expose] def freeRigidPresentation :
    MonoidalCore.Presentation.{u, max u v} where
  Obj := RigidObject S.Obj
  unitObj := RigidObject.unit
  tensorObj := RigidObject.tensor
  Gen := FreeRigidGen S
  Rel := FreeRigidRel S

/-- The free rigid monoidal category on a duality signature `S`. Its objects are the formal
rigid objects in the generating objects of `S`. -/
abbrev FreeRigid : Type u :=
  MonoidalCore.Free (freeRigidPresentation S)

namespace FreeRigid

variable {S}

/-- Construct an object of `S.FreeRigid` from a formal rigid object. -/
abbrev mk (as : RigidObject S.Obj) : S.FreeRigid := ⟨as⟩

/-- Extract the underlying formal rigid object of an object of `S.FreeRigid`. -/
abbrev as (X : S.FreeRigid) : RigidObject S.Obj := MonoidalCore.Free.as X

/-- The object of the free rigid monoidal category given by a single generating object. -/
@[expose] def of (a : S.Obj) : S.FreeRigid := ⟨.of a⟩

/-- Distinct generating objects produce distinct objects of `S.FreeRigid`. -/
@[simp]
theorem of_inj {a b : S.Obj} : of a = of b ↔ a = b :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ by cases h; rfl, congrArg of⟩

/-- Formal composites, tensor products and whiskerings of identities, associators, unitors,
evaluations and coevaluations of the formal right and left duals, and coupons. The morphisms of
`S.FreeRigid` are the quotient of these by `MonoidalCore.HomEquiv (FreeRigidRel S)`. -/
abbrev Hom (X Y : RigidObject S.Obj) : Type (max u v) :=
  MonoidalCore.Hom RigidObject.unit RigidObject.tensor (FreeRigidGen S) X Y

/-- The formal evaluation `Xᘁ ⊗ X ⟶ 𝟙` of the formal right dual. -/
@[match_pattern] abbrev Hom.εRight (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    Hom (S := S) (X.rightDual.tensor X) .unit :=
  MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.ε_right X)

/-- The formal coevaluation `𝟙 ⟶ X ⊗ Xᘁ` of the formal right dual. -/
@[match_pattern] abbrev Hom.ηRight (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    Hom (S := S) .unit (X.tensor X.rightDual) :=
  MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.η_right X)

/-- The formal evaluation `X ⊗ ᘁX ⟶ 𝟙` of the formal left dual. -/
@[match_pattern] abbrev Hom.εLeft (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    Hom (S := S) (X.tensor X.leftDual) .unit :=
  MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.ε_left X)

/-- The formal coevaluation `𝟙 ⟶ ᘁX ⊗ X` of the formal left dual. -/
@[match_pattern] abbrev Hom.ηLeft (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    Hom (S := S) .unit (X.leftDual.tensor X) :=
  MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.η_left X)

/-- The formal morphism given by a coupon `g` of `S`. -/
@[match_pattern] abbrev Hom.coupon (g : S.Coupon) : Hom (S := S) (S.src g) (S.tgt g) :=
  MonoidalCore.Hom.gen (.coupon g)

/-- The morphism of the free rigid monoidal category represented by a formal morphism. -/
abbrev homMk {X Y : S.FreeRigid} (f : Hom (S := S) X.as Y.as) : X ⟶ Y :=
  MonoidalCore.homMk f

/-- The chosen right dual of an object of `S.FreeRigid` is its formal right dual, with the
formal evaluation and coevaluation. -/
instance : RightRigidCategory S.FreeRigid where
  rightDual X :=
    { rightDual := ⟨X.as.rightDual⟩
      exact :=
        { coevaluation' := homMk (X := 𝟙_ _) (Y := X ⊗ ⟨X.as.rightDual⟩) (Hom.ηRight X.as)
          evaluation' := homMk (X := ⟨X.as.rightDual⟩ ⊗ X) (Y := 𝟙_ _) (Hom.εRight X.as)
          coevaluation_evaluation' := Quotient.sound (.extra .right_coevaluation_evaluation)
          evaluation_coevaluation' := Quotient.sound (.extra .right_evaluation_coevaluation) } }

/-- The chosen left dual of an object of `S.FreeRigid` is its formal left dual, with the formal
evaluation and coevaluation. -/
instance : LeftRigidCategory S.FreeRigid where
  leftDual X :=
    { leftDual := ⟨X.as.leftDual⟩
      exact :=
        { coevaluation' := homMk (X := 𝟙_ _) (Y := ⟨X.as.leftDual⟩ ⊗ X) (Hom.ηLeft X.as)
          evaluation' := homMk (X := X ⊗ ⟨X.as.leftDual⟩) (Y := 𝟙_ _) (Hom.εLeft X.as)
          coevaluation_evaluation' := Quotient.sound (.extra .left_coevaluation_evaluation)
          evaluation_coevaluation' := Quotient.sound (.extra .left_evaluation_coevaluation) } }

/-- `S.FreeRigid` is rigid, with the formal right and left duals as chosen duals. -/
instance : RigidCategory S.FreeRigid where

-- `no_index S.Obj` ensures `simp` also matches concrete `abbrev` signatures whose `Obj` reduces,
-- and `rfl` (without parentheses) lets `dsimp` apply these rules inside dependent arguments such
-- as `FreeRigid.wordIso`.
/-- Wrapping the formal unit gives `𝟙_ S.FreeRigid`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mk_unit : (⟨.unit⟩ : S.FreeRigid) = 𝟙_ S.FreeRigid := rfl

/-- Wrapping a formal tensor product gives the tensor product in `S.FreeRigid`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mk_tensor (X Y : RigidObject (no_index S.Obj)) :
    (⟨X.tensor Y⟩ : S.FreeRigid) = ⟨X⟩ ⊗ ⟨Y⟩ := rfl

/-- Wrapping a formal right dual gives the chosen right dual in `S.FreeRigid`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mk_rightDual (X : RigidObject (no_index S.Obj)) :
    (⟨X.rightDual⟩ : S.FreeRigid) = (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)ᘁ := rfl

/-- Wrapping a formal left dual gives the chosen left dual in `S.FreeRigid`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mk_leftDual (X : RigidObject (no_index S.Obj)) :
    (⟨X.leftDual⟩ : S.FreeRigid) = (ᘁ(⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid) : S.FreeRigid) := rfl

/-- The chosen right dual of `X` in `S.FreeRigid` is the formal right dual expression. -/
theorem rightDual_eq (X : S.FreeRigid) : Xᘁ = ⟨X.as.rightDual⟩ := rfl

/-- The chosen left dual of `X` in `S.FreeRigid` is the formal left dual expression. -/
theorem leftDual_eq (X : S.FreeRigid) : (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) = ⟨X.as.leftDual⟩ := rfl

/-- Double right duality does not identify a generating object with itself in `S.FreeRigid`. -/
theorem of_ne_doubleRightDual (a : S.Obj) : (of a : S.FreeRigid) ≠ ((of a : S.FreeRigid)ᘁ)ᘁ := by
  intro h
  rw [rightDual_eq, rightDual_eq] at h
  exact RigidObject.normalize_rightDual_rightDual_ne a
    (congrArg (RigidObject.normalize ∘ FreeRigid.as) h).symm

/-- Evaluating a formal rigid object in `S.FreeRigid` at the generating objects recovers the object
itself. -/
@[simp]
theorem eval_of (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    RigidObject.eval (of (S := S)) X = ⟨X⟩ := by
  induction X with
  | of a => rfl
  | unit => rfl
  | tensor X Y ihX ihY => simp only [RigidObject.eval_tensor, ihX, ihY, mk_tensor]
  | rightDual X ih => simp only [RigidObject.eval_rightDual, ih, rightDual_eq]
  | leftDual X ih => simp only [RigidObject.eval_leftDual, ih, leftDual_eq]

/-- The generating morphism given by a coupon, from its source to its target. -/
@[expose] def coupon (g : S.Coupon) : (⟨S.src g⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ⟶ ⟨S.tgt g⟩ :=
  homMk (Hom.coupon g)

/-- `Hom.εRight` represents the evaluation of the chosen right dual. -/
@[simp]
theorem homMk_ε_right (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := Xᘁ ⊗ X) (Y := 𝟙_ _) (Hom.εRight X.as) = ε_ X Xᘁ := (rfl)

/-- `Hom.ηRight` represents the coevaluation of the chosen right dual. -/
@[simp]
theorem homMk_η_right (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := 𝟙_ _) (Y := X ⊗ Xᘁ) (Hom.ηRight X.as) = η_ X Xᘁ := (rfl)

/-- `Hom.εLeft` represents the evaluation of the chosen left dual. -/
@[simp]
theorem homMk_ε_left (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := X ⊗ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid)) (Y := 𝟙_ _) (Hom.εLeft X.as) =
      ε_ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X := (rfl)

/-- `Hom.ηLeft` represents the coevaluation of the chosen left dual. -/
@[simp]
theorem homMk_η_left (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := 𝟙_ _) (Y := (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) ⊗ X) (Hom.ηLeft X.as) =
      η_ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X := (rfl)

/-- `Hom.coupon g` represents `coupon g`. -/
@[simp]
theorem homMk_coupon (g : S.Coupon) :
    homMk (X := ⟨S.src g⟩) (Y := ⟨S.tgt g⟩) (Hom.coupon g) = coupon g := (rfl)

/-- Induction principle for morphisms of the free rigid monoidal category: a property of
morphisms holding for identities, associators, unitors, evaluations and coevaluations of the
chosen right and left duals, and coupons, and stable under composition and whiskering on either
side, holds for every morphism. -/
theorem Hom.inductionOn {motive : {X Y : S.FreeRigid} → (X ⟶ Y) → Prop} {X Y : S.FreeRigid}
    (t : X ⟶ Y)
    (id : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (𝟙 X))
    (α_hom : (X Y Z : S.FreeRigid) → motive (α_ X Y Z).hom)
    (α_inv : (X Y Z : S.FreeRigid) → motive (α_ X Y Z).inv)
    (l_hom : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (λ_ X).hom)
    (l_inv : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (λ_ X).inv)
    (ρ_hom : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (ρ_ X).hom)
    (ρ_inv : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (ρ_ X).inv)
    (ε_right : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (ε_ X Xᘁ))
    (η_right : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (η_ X Xᘁ))
    (ε_left : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (ε_ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X))
    (η_left : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (η_ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X))
    (coupon : (g : S.Coupon) → motive (FreeRigid.coupon g))
    (comp : {X Y Z : S.FreeRigid} → (f : X ⟶ Y) → (g : Y ⟶ Z) → motive f → motive g →
      motive (f ≫ g))
    (whiskerLeft : (X : S.FreeRigid) → {Y Z : S.FreeRigid} → (f : Y ⟶ Z) → motive f →
      motive (X ◁ f))
    (whiskerRight : {X Y : S.FreeRigid} → (f : X ⟶ Y) → (Z : S.FreeRigid) → motive f →
      motive (f ▷ Z)) :
    motive t :=
  MonoidalCore.Hom.inductionOn t id α_hom α_inv l_hom l_inv ρ_hom ρ_inv
    (fun
      | .ε_right X => ε_right ⟨X⟩
      | .η_right X => η_right ⟨X⟩
      | .ε_left X => ε_left ⟨X⟩
      | .η_left X => η_left ⟨X⟩
      | .coupon g => coupon g)
    comp whiskerLeft whiskerRight

section Lift

variable {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] [MonoidalCategory D] [RigidCategory D]
  (fo : S.Obj → D)
  (fc : ∀ g : S.Coupon, RigidObject.eval fo (S.src g) ⟶ RigidObject.eval fo (S.tgt g))

/-- Images of the duality and coupon generators of `S.FreeRigid` under `lift fo fc`. -/
@[expose] def liftGen :
    ∀ {X Y : RigidObject S.Obj}, FreeRigidGen S X Y →
      (RigidObject.eval fo X ⟶ RigidObject.eval fo Y)
  | _, _, .ε_right X => ε_ (RigidObject.eval fo X) (RigidObject.eval fo X)ᘁ
  | _, _, .η_right X => η_ (RigidObject.eval fo X) (RigidObject.eval fo X)ᘁ
  | _, _, .ε_left X => ε_ (ᘁ(RigidObject.eval fo X)) (RigidObject.eval fo X)
  | _, _, .η_left X => η_ (ᘁ(RigidObject.eval fo X)) (RigidObject.eval fo X)
  | _, _, .coupon g => fc g

/-- Soundness of `liftGen` with respect to the zigzag relations `FreeRigidRel S`. -/
theorem lift_hrel :
    ∀ {X Y : RigidObject S.Obj}
      {f g : MonoidalCore.Hom RigidObject.unit RigidObject.tensor (FreeRigidGen S) X Y},
      FreeRigidRel S f g →
        MonoidalCore.liftMapAux
          (MonoidalCore.MonoidalEval.ofMonoidal (RigidObject.eval fo) rfl fun _ _ ↦ rfl)
          (liftGen fo fc) f =
        MonoidalCore.liftMapAux
          (MonoidalCore.MonoidalEval.ofMonoidal (RigidObject.eval fo) rfl fun _ _ ↦ rfl)
          (liftGen fo fc) g := by
  rintro _ _ _ _ (⟨X⟩ | ⟨X⟩ | ⟨X⟩ | ⟨X⟩)
  · simp only [MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_comp, MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_whiskerLeft,
      MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_α_inv, MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_whiskerRight,
      MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_gen, MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_ρ_hom,
      MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_l_inv, MonoidalCore.MonoidalEval.ofMonoidal,
      RigidObject.eval, liftGen]
    exact ExactPairing.coevaluation_evaluation _ _
  · simp only [MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_comp, MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_whiskerRight,
      MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_α_hom, MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_whiskerLeft,
      MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_gen, MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_l_hom,
      MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_ρ_inv, MonoidalCore.MonoidalEval.ofMonoidal,
      RigidObject.eval, liftGen]
    exact ExactPairing.evaluation_coevaluation _ _
  · simp only [MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_comp, MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_whiskerLeft,
      MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_α_inv, MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_whiskerRight,
      MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_gen, MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_ρ_hom,
      MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_l_inv, MonoidalCore.MonoidalEval.ofMonoidal,
      RigidObject.eval, liftGen]
    exact ExactPairing.coevaluation_evaluation _ _
  · simp only [MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_comp, MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_whiskerRight,
      MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_α_hom, MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_whiskerLeft,
      MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_gen, MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_l_hom,
      MonoidalCore.liftMapAux_ρ_inv, MonoidalCore.MonoidalEval.ofMonoidal,
      RigidObject.eval, liftGen]
    exact ExactPairing.evaluation_coevaluation _ _

-- The body is exposed so that the object part reduces, as for `TensorSignature.FreeMonoidal.lift`:
-- the statements of `lift_ε` and its companions only typecheck once `(lift fo fc).obj X` reduces
-- to the corresponding tensor product or dual in `D`.
/-- The functor out of the free rigid monoidal category on `S` determined by the images `fo` of
the generating objects and `fc` of the coupons. It is strong monoidal, with identity tensorator
and unit comparison, and sends the chosen duals of `S.FreeRigid` to the chosen duals of `D`. -/
@[expose] def lift : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D :=
  MonoidalCore.lift
    (MonoidalCore.MonoidalEval.ofMonoidal (RigidObject.eval fo) rfl fun _ _ ↦ rfl)
    (MonoidalCore.MonoidalEval.ofMonoidal_lawful (RigidObject.eval fo) rfl fun _ _ ↦ rfl)
    (liftGen fo fc) (lift_hrel fo fc)

/-- On objects, `lift fo fc` evaluates the underlying formal rigid object. -/
theorem lift_obj (X : S.FreeRigid) : (lift fo fc).obj X = RigidObject.eval fo X.as := rfl

/-- `lift fo fc` sends each generating object `of a` to `fo a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_obj_of (a : S.Obj) : (lift fo fc).obj (of a) = fo a := rfl

/-- `lift fo fc` preserves tensor products of objects strictly. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_obj_tensor (X Y : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).obj (X ⊗ Y) = (lift fo fc).obj X ⊗ (lift fo fc).obj Y := rfl

/-- `lift fo fc` preserves the tensor unit strictly. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_obj_tensorUnit : (lift fo fc).obj (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid) = 𝟙_ D := rfl

/-- `lift fo fc` sends the chosen right dual to the chosen right dual. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_obj_rightDual (X : S.FreeRigid) : (lift fo fc).obj Xᘁ = ((lift fo fc).obj X)ᘁ := rfl

/-- `lift fo fc` sends the chosen left dual to the chosen left dual. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_obj_leftDual (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).obj (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) = (ᘁ((lift fo fc).obj X) : D) := rfl

/-- `lift fo fc` sends each coupon `g` to `fc g`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_map_coupon (g : S.Coupon) : (lift fo fc).map (coupon g) = fc g :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_gen (P := freeRigidPresentation S) (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) (.coupon g)

/-- `lift fo fc` preserves left whiskering strictly. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_map_whiskerLeft (X : S.FreeRigid) {Y₁ Y₂ : S.FreeRigid} (f : Y₁ ⟶ Y₂) :
    (lift fo fc).map (X ◁ f) = (lift fo fc).obj X ◁ (lift fo fc).map f :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_whiskerLeft (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) X f

/-- `lift fo fc` preserves right whiskering strictly. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_map_whiskerRight {X₁ X₂ : S.FreeRigid} (f : X₁ ⟶ X₂) (Y : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (f ▷ Y) = (lift fo fc).map f ▷ (lift fo fc).obj Y :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_whiskerRight (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) f Y

/-- `lift fo fc` preserves tensor products of morphisms strictly. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_map_tensorHom {X₁ Y₁ X₂ Y₂ : S.FreeRigid} (f : X₁ ⟶ Y₁) (g : X₂ ⟶ Y₂) :
    (lift fo fc).map (f ⊗ₘ g) = (lift fo fc).map f ⊗ₘ (lift fo fc).map g :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_tensorHom (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) f g

/-- `lift fo fc` sends the forward associator to the forward associator of `D`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_map_associator_hom (X Y Z : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (α_ X Y Z).hom =
      (α_ ((lift fo fc).obj X) ((lift fo fc).obj Y) ((lift fo fc).obj Z)).hom :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_associator_hom (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) X Y Z

/-- `lift fo fc` sends the inverse associator to the inverse associator of `D`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_map_associator_inv (X Y Z : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (α_ X Y Z).inv =
      (α_ ((lift fo fc).obj X) ((lift fo fc).obj Y) ((lift fo fc).obj Z)).inv :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_associator_inv (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) X Y Z

/- The unitor lemmas are not `@[simp]`: `Functor.LaxMonoidal` unitality lemmas rewrite unitors
back into `map` of a unitor. -/

/-- `lift fo fc` sends the forward left unitor to the forward left unitor of `D`. -/
theorem lift_map_leftUnitor_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (λ_ X).hom = (λ_ ((lift fo fc).obj X)).hom :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_leftUnitor_hom (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) X

/-- `lift fo fc` sends the inverse left unitor to the inverse left unitor of `D`. -/
theorem lift_map_leftUnitor_inv (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (λ_ X).inv = (λ_ ((lift fo fc).obj X)).inv :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_leftUnitor_inv (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) X

/-- `lift fo fc` sends the forward right unitor to the forward right unitor of `D`. -/
theorem lift_map_rightUnitor_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (ρ_ X).hom = (ρ_ ((lift fo fc).obj X)).hom :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_rightUnitor_hom (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) X

/-- `lift fo fc` sends the inverse right unitor to the inverse right unitor of `D`. -/
theorem lift_map_rightUnitor_inv (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (ρ_ X).inv = (ρ_ ((lift fo fc).obj X)).inv :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_rightUnitor_inv (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) X

/-- `lift fo fc` sends the evaluation of the chosen right dual to that of `D`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_map_evaluation_rightDual (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (ε_ X Xᘁ) = ε_ ((lift fo fc).obj X) ((lift fo fc).obj X)ᘁ :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_gen (P := freeRigidPresentation S) (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) (.ε_right X.as)

/-- `lift fo fc` sends the coevaluation of the chosen right dual to that of `D`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_map_coevaluation_rightDual (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (η_ X Xᘁ) = η_ ((lift fo fc).obj X) ((lift fo fc).obj X)ᘁ :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_gen (P := freeRigidPresentation S) (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) (.η_right X.as)

/-- `lift fo fc` sends the evaluation of the chosen left dual to that of `D`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_map_evaluation_leftDual (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (ε_ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X) =
      ε_ (ᘁ((lift fo fc).obj X)) ((lift fo fc).obj X) :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_gen (P := freeRigidPresentation S) (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) (.ε_left X.as)

/-- `lift fo fc` sends the coevaluation of the chosen left dual to that of `D`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_map_coevaluation_leftDual (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (η_ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X) =
      η_ (ᘁ((lift fo fc).obj X)) ((lift fo fc).obj X) :=
  MonoidalCore.lift_map_gen (P := freeRigidPresentation S) (hrel := lift_hrel fo fc) (.η_left X.as)

/-- `lift fo fc` is strong monoidal, with identity unit comparison and tensorator. -/
instance : (lift fo fc).Monoidal :=
  Functor.CoreMonoidal.toMonoidal
    { εIso := Iso.refl _
      μIso := fun _ _ ↦ Iso.refl _
      μIso_hom_natural_left := by
        intros
        dsimp only [Iso.refl_hom, lift_obj_tensor]
        simp
      μIso_hom_natural_right := by
        intros
        dsimp only [Iso.refl_hom, lift_obj_tensor]
        simp
      associativity := by
        intros
        dsimp only [Iso.refl_hom, lift_obj_tensor]
        simp
      left_unitality := by
        intros
        dsimp only [Iso.refl_hom, lift_obj_tensor, lift_obj_tensorUnit]
        simp [lift_map_leftUnitor_hom]
      right_unitality := by
        intros
        dsimp only [Iso.refl_hom, lift_obj_tensor, lift_obj_tensorUnit]
        simp [lift_map_rightUnitor_hom] }

/-- The unit morphism of `lift fo fc` is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_ε : Functor.LaxMonoidal.ε (lift fo fc) = 𝟙 _ := (rfl)

/-- The counit morphism of `lift fo fc` is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_η : Functor.OplaxMonoidal.η (lift fo fc) = 𝟙 _ := (rfl)

/-- The tensorator of `lift fo fc` is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_μ (X Y : S.FreeRigid) : Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ (lift fo fc) X Y = 𝟙 _ := (rfl)

/-- The inverse tensorator of `lift fo fc` is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_δ (X Y : S.FreeRigid) : Functor.OplaxMonoidal.δ (lift fo fc) X Y = 𝟙 _ := (rfl)

/-- The comparison between the image of the chosen right dual under `lift fo fc` and the chosen
right dual of the image is the identity: `lift fo fc` preserves chosen right duals on the nose. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_mapRightDualIso (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).mapRightDualIso X = Iso.refl _ := by
  ext
  refine ExactPairing.rightHom_ext (X := (lift fo fc).obj X) ?_
  rw [Functor.mapRightDualIso_hom_whiskerRight_evaluation]
  simp

/-- The comparison between the image of the chosen left dual under `lift fo fc` and the chosen
left dual of the image is the identity: `lift fo fc` preserves chosen left duals on the nose. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_mapLeftDualIso (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).mapLeftDualIso X = Iso.refl _ := by
  ext
  refine ExactPairing.leftDualHom_ext (Y := (lift fo fc).obj X) ?_
  rw [Functor.whiskerLeft_mapLeftDualIso_hom_evaluation]
  simp

end Lift

section CouponCount

open scoped SingleObj

private noncomputable def countLift (g₀ : S.Coupon) :
    S.FreeRigid ⥤ SingleObj (Multiplicative ℕ) :=
  lift (fun _ ↦ SingleObj.star _)
    (fun g ↦ @ite _ (g = g₀) (Classical.propDecidable _)
      (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1) (Multiplicative.ofAdd 0))

/-- The number of occurrences of a coupon `g₀` in a morphism of `S.FreeRigid`. This is invariant
under the rigid-category axioms, because every monoidal and zigzag relation is balanced in every
coupon. -/
noncomputable def couponCount (g₀ : S.Coupon) {X Y : S.FreeRigid} (f : X ⟶ Y) : ℕ :=
  Multiplicative.toAdd ((countLift g₀).map f)

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_id (g₀ : S.Coupon) (X : S.FreeRigid) : couponCount g₀ (𝟙 X) = 0 := by
  simp [couponCount, SingleObj.id_as_one]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_associator_hom (g₀ : S.Coupon) (X Y Z : S.FreeRigid) :
    couponCount g₀ (α_ X Y Z).hom = 0 := by
  simp [couponCount, countLift, SingleObj.id_as_one]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_associator_inv (g₀ : S.Coupon) (X Y Z : S.FreeRigid) :
    couponCount g₀ (α_ X Y Z).inv = 0 := by
  simp [couponCount, countLift, SingleObj.id_as_one]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_leftUnitor_hom (g₀ : S.Coupon) (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    couponCount g₀ (λ_ X).hom = 0 := by
  rw [couponCount, countLift, lift_map_leftUnitor_hom]
  simp [SingleObj.id_as_one]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_leftUnitor_inv (g₀ : S.Coupon) (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    couponCount g₀ (λ_ X).inv = 0 := by
  rw [couponCount, countLift, lift_map_leftUnitor_inv]
  simp [SingleObj.id_as_one]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_rightUnitor_hom (g₀ : S.Coupon) (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    couponCount g₀ (ρ_ X).hom = 0 := by
  rw [couponCount, countLift, lift_map_rightUnitor_hom]
  simp [SingleObj.id_as_one]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_rightUnitor_inv (g₀ : S.Coupon) (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    couponCount g₀ (ρ_ X).inv = 0 := by
  rw [couponCount, countLift, lift_map_rightUnitor_inv]
  simp [SingleObj.id_as_one]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_coevaluation_rightDual (g₀ : S.Coupon) (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    couponCount g₀ (η_ X Xᘁ) = 0 := by
  simp [couponCount, countLift]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_evaluation_rightDual (g₀ : S.Coupon) (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    couponCount g₀ (ε_ X Xᘁ) = 0 := by
  simp [couponCount, countLift]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_coevaluation_leftDual (g₀ : S.Coupon) (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    couponCount g₀ (η_ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X) = 0 := by
  simp [couponCount, countLift]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_evaluation_leftDual (g₀ : S.Coupon) (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    couponCount g₀ (ε_ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X) = 0 := by
  simp [couponCount, countLift]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_comp (g₀ : S.Coupon) {X Y Z : S.FreeRigid} (f : X ⟶ Y) (g : Y ⟶ Z) :
    couponCount g₀ (f ≫ g) = couponCount g₀ f + couponCount g₀ g := by
  simp only [couponCount, Functor.map_comp, SingleObj.comp_as_mul]
  exact (toAdd_mul _ _).trans (Nat.add_comm _ _)

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_whiskerLeft (g₀ : S.Coupon) (X : S.FreeRigid) {Y₁ Y₂ : S.FreeRigid}
    (f : Y₁ ⟶ Y₂) : couponCount g₀ (X ◁ f) = couponCount g₀ f := by
  simp only [couponCount, countLift, lift_map_whiskerLeft, SingleObj.whiskerLeft_eq]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_whiskerRight (g₀ : S.Coupon) {X₁ X₂ : S.FreeRigid} (f : X₁ ⟶ X₂)
    (Y : S.FreeRigid) : couponCount g₀ (f ▷ Y) = couponCount g₀ f := by
  simp only [couponCount, countLift, lift_map_whiskerRight, SingleObj.whiskerRight_eq]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_tensorHom (g₀ : S.Coupon) {X₁ Y₁ X₂ Y₂ : S.FreeRigid} (f : X₁ ⟶ Y₁)
    (g : X₂ ⟶ Y₂) : couponCount g₀ (f ⊗ₘ g) = couponCount g₀ f + couponCount g₀ g := by
  rw [couponCount, countLift, lift_map_tensorHom, SingleObj.tensorHom_as_mul]
  exact toAdd_mul _ _

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_coupon_self (g : S.Coupon) : couponCount g (coupon g) = 1 := by
  simp [couponCount, countLift]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_coupon_of_ne {g₁ g₂ : S.Coupon} (h : g₂ ≠ g₁) :
    couponCount g₁ (coupon g₂) = 0 := by
  simp [couponCount, countLift, h]

@[simp]
theorem couponCount_eqToHom (g₀ : S.Coupon) {X Y : S.FreeRigid} (h : X = Y) :
    couponCount g₀ (eqToHom h) = 0 := by subst h; exact couponCount_id g₀ X

/-- No coupon is identified with an identity morphism in `S.FreeRigid`. In particular, a nullary
coupon `𝟙_ S.FreeRigid ⟶ 𝟙_ S.FreeRigid` is distinct from `𝟙 (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid)`. -/
theorem coupon_ne_id (g : S.Coupon) (h : S.src g = S.tgt g) :
    coupon g ≠ eqToHom (congrArg FreeRigid.mk h) := by
  intro heq
  have hc := congrArg (couponCount g) heq
  simp at hc

/-- Distinct coupons with matching boundaries remain distinct morphisms in `S.FreeRigid`. -/
theorem coupon_ne_coupon {g₁ g₂ : S.Coupon} (hsrc : S.src g₁ = S.src g₂)
    (htgt : S.tgt g₁ = S.tgt g₂) (hne : g₁ ≠ g₂) :
    coupon g₁ ≠
      eqToHom (congrArg FreeRigid.mk hsrc) ≫ coupon g₂ ≫
        eqToHom (congrArg FreeRigid.mk htgt.symm) := by
  intro heq
  have hc := congrArg (couponCount g₁) heq
  simp [hne.symm] at hc

end CouponCount

section Uniqueness

open Functor.LaxMonoidal Functor.OplaxMonoidal

variable {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] [MonoidalCategory D]

/-- A monoidal natural transformation between strong monoidal functors out of the free rigid
monoidal category on `S` is determined by its components at the generating objects. -/
theorem natTrans_ext {F G : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D} [F.Monoidal] [G.Monoidal] {α β : F ⟶ G}
    [NatTrans.IsMonoidal α] [NatTrans.IsMonoidal β] (h : ∀ a, α.app (of a) = β.app (of a)) :
    α = β := by
  ext ⟨X⟩
  induction X with
  | of a => exact h a
  | unit => exact NatTrans.IsMonoidal.app_tensorUnit_eq
  | tensor X Y hX hY => exact NatTrans.IsMonoidal.app_tensor_eq hX hY
  | rightDual X hX => exact NatTrans.app_right_eq_of_app_left_eq α β ⟨X⟩ ⟨X⟩ᘁ hX
  | leftDual X hX => exact NatTrans.app_left_eq_of_app_right_eq α β (ᘁ⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ⟨X⟩ hX

variable (F G : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D) [F.Monoidal] [G.Monoidal] (e : ∀ a, F.obj (of a) ≅ G.obj (of a))

/-- The isomorphism between the images of a formal rigid object under two strong monoidal
functors out of the free rigid monoidal category, induced by isomorphisms `e` at the generating
objects together with the tensorators and unit comparisons of the two functors. At a dual it is
the mate, with respect to the image pairings, of the inverse of the isomorphism at the object. -/
def wordIso : ∀ X : RigidObject S.Obj, F.obj ⟨X⟩ ≅ G.obj ⟨X⟩
  | .of a => e a
  | .unit => Functor.Monoidal.isoAppUnit F G
  | .tensor X Y => Functor.Monoidal.isoAppTensor F G (wordIso X) (wordIso Y)
  | .rightDual X =>
    { hom := ExactPairing.rightMate (G.mapExactPairing ⟨X⟩ ⟨X⟩ᘁ) (F.mapExactPairing ⟨X⟩ ⟨X⟩ᘁ)
        (wordIso X).inv
      inv := ExactPairing.rightMate (F.mapExactPairing ⟨X⟩ ⟨X⟩ᘁ) (G.mapExactPairing ⟨X⟩ ⟨X⟩ᘁ)
        (wordIso X).hom
      hom_inv_id := by
        rw [← ExactPairing.comp_rightMate, Iso.hom_inv_id, ExactPairing.rightMate_id]
      inv_hom_id := by
        rw [← ExactPairing.comp_rightMate, Iso.inv_hom_id, ExactPairing.rightMate_id] }
  | .leftDual X =>
    { hom := ExactPairing.leftMate (G.mapExactPairing (ᘁ⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ⟨X⟩)
        (F.mapExactPairing (ᘁ⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ⟨X⟩) (wordIso X).inv
      inv := ExactPairing.leftMate (F.mapExactPairing (ᘁ⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ⟨X⟩)
        (G.mapExactPairing (ᘁ⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ⟨X⟩) (wordIso X).hom
      hom_inv_id := by
        rw [← ExactPairing.comp_leftMate, Iso.hom_inv_id, ExactPairing.leftMate_id]
      inv_hom_id := by
        rw [← ExactPairing.comp_leftMate, Iso.inv_hom_id, ExactPairing.leftMate_id] }

/-- At a generating object, `wordIso F G e` is the given isomorphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem wordIso_of (a : S.Obj) : wordIso F G e (of a).as = e a := by rfl

/-- At the unit, `wordIso F G e` is built from the unit comparisons of `F` and `G`. -/
@[simp]
theorem wordIso_tensorUnit_hom : (wordIso F G e (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as).hom = η F ≫ ε G :=
  Functor.Monoidal.isoAppUnit_hom F G

/-- At a tensor product, `wordIso F G e` is the tensor product of its values at the factors,
conjugated by the tensorators of `F` and `G`. -/
@[simp]
theorem wordIso_tensor_hom (X Y : S.FreeRigid) :
    (wordIso F G e (X ⊗ Y).as).hom =
      δ F X Y ≫ ((wordIso F G e X.as).hom ⊗ₘ (wordIso F G e Y.as).hom) ≫ μ G X Y :=
  Functor.Monoidal.isoAppTensor_hom F G _ _

/-- At a right dual, `wordIso F G e` is the mate of the inverse of its value at the object, with
respect to the image pairings. -/
@[simp]
theorem wordIso_rightDual_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (wordIso F G e Xᘁ.as).hom = ExactPairing.rightMate (G.mapExactPairing X Xᘁ)
      (F.mapExactPairing X Xᘁ) (wordIso F G e X.as).inv := by rfl

/-- The inverse of `wordIso F G e` at a right dual is the mate of its value at the object. -/
@[simp]
theorem wordIso_rightDual_inv (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (wordIso F G e Xᘁ.as).inv = ExactPairing.rightMate (F.mapExactPairing X Xᘁ)
      (G.mapExactPairing X Xᘁ) (wordIso F G e X.as).hom := by rfl

/-- At a left dual, `wordIso F G e` is the left mate of the inverse of its value at the object,
with respect to the image pairings. -/
@[simp]
theorem wordIso_leftDual_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (wordIso F G e (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid).as).hom =
      ExactPairing.leftMate (G.mapExactPairing (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X)
        (F.mapExactPairing (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X) (wordIso F G e X.as).inv := by rfl

/-- The inverse of `wordIso F G e` at a left dual is the left mate of its value at the object. -/
@[simp]
theorem wordIso_leftDual_inv (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (wordIso F G e (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid).as).inv =
      ExactPairing.leftMate (F.mapExactPairing (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X)
        (G.mapExactPairing (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X) (wordIso F G e X.as).hom := by rfl

variable {F G e}

/- In the duality cases of `map_comp_wordIso_hom`, the mate of the inverse of `wordIso` at `X`
tensored with `wordIso` at `X` carries one image evaluation (or coevaluation) to the other by the
defining property of the mate, and
`Functor.map_{evaluation,coevaluation}_naturality_of_mapExactPairing` lifts that to naturality up
to the functor comparisons. -/

private theorem map_evaluation_rightDual_comp_wordIso_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    F.map (ε_ X Xᘁ) ≫ (wordIso F G e (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as).hom =
      (wordIso F G e (Xᘁ ⊗ X).as).hom ≫ G.map (ε_ X Xᘁ) := by
  rw [wordIso_tensorUnit_hom, wordIso_tensor_hom]
  refine Functor.map_evaluation_naturality_of_mapExactPairing ?_
  rw [wordIso_rightDual_hom, tensorHom_def', Category.assoc,
    ExactPairing.rightMate_comp_evaluation, ← whiskerLeft_comp_assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id,
    MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_id, Category.id_comp]

private theorem map_coevaluation_rightDual_comp_wordIso_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    F.map (η_ X Xᘁ) ≫ (wordIso F G e (X ⊗ Xᘁ).as).hom =
      (wordIso F G e (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as).hom ≫ G.map (η_ X Xᘁ) := by
  rw [wordIso_tensor_hom, wordIso_tensorUnit_hom]
  refine Functor.map_coevaluation_naturality_of_mapExactPairing ?_
  rw [wordIso_rightDual_hom, tensorHom_def',
    ExactPairing.coevaluation_comp_rightMate_assoc, ← comp_whiskerRight, Iso.inv_hom_id,
    MonoidalCategory.id_whiskerRight, Category.comp_id]

private theorem map_evaluation_leftDual_comp_wordIso_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    F.map (ε_ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X) ≫ (wordIso F G e (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as).hom =
      (wordIso F G e (X ⊗ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid)).as).hom ≫ G.map (ε_ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X) := by
  rw [wordIso_tensorUnit_hom, wordIso_tensor_hom]
  refine Functor.map_evaluation_naturality_of_mapExactPairing ?_
  rw [wordIso_leftDual_hom, MonoidalCategory.tensorHom_def, Category.assoc,
    ExactPairing.leftMate_comp_evaluation, ← comp_whiskerRight_assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id,
    MonoidalCategory.id_whiskerRight, Category.id_comp]

private theorem map_coevaluation_leftDual_comp_wordIso_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    F.map (η_ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X) ≫ (wordIso F G e ((ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) ⊗ X).as).hom =
      (wordIso F G e (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as).hom ≫ G.map (η_ (ᘁX : S.FreeRigid) X) := by
  rw [wordIso_tensor_hom, wordIso_tensorUnit_hom]
  refine Functor.map_coevaluation_naturality_of_mapExactPairing ?_
  rw [wordIso_leftDual_hom, MonoidalCategory.tensorHom_def,
    ExactPairing.coevaluation_comp_leftMate_assoc, ← whiskerLeft_comp, Iso.inv_hom_id,
    MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_id, Category.comp_id]

/-- The isomorphisms `wordIso F G e` are natural as soon as they are natural with respect to
the coupons. -/
theorem map_comp_wordIso_hom
    (he : ∀ g, F.map (coupon g) ≫ (wordIso F G e (S.tgt g)).hom =
      (wordIso F G e (S.src g)).hom ≫ G.map (coupon g))
    {X Y : S.FreeRigid} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    F.map f ≫ (wordIso F G e Y.as).hom = (wordIso F G e X.as).hom ≫ G.map f := by
  have hunit : (wordIso F G e (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as).hom = η F ≫ ε G :=
    wordIso_tensorUnit_hom F G e
  have htensor : ∀ A B : S.FreeRigid,
      (wordIso F G e (A ⊗ B).as).hom =
        δ F A B ≫ ((wordIso F G e A.as).hom ⊗ₘ (wordIso F G e B.as).hom) ≫ μ G A B :=
    wordIso_tensor_hom F G e
  induction f using Hom.inductionOn with
  | id X => simp
  | α_hom X Y Z =>
    exact Functor.Monoidal.associator_hom_naturality_of_tensor
      (e := fun Z ↦ (wordIso F G e Z.as).hom) htensor X Y Z
  | α_inv X Y Z =>
    exact (CommSq.horiz_inv (f := F.mapIso (α_ X Y Z)) (i := G.mapIso (α_ X Y Z))
      ⟨Functor.Monoidal.associator_hom_naturality_of_tensor
        (e := fun Z ↦ (wordIso F G e Z.as).hom) htensor X Y Z⟩).w
  | l_hom X =>
    exact Functor.Monoidal.leftUnitor_hom_naturality_of_unit_tensor
      (e := fun Z ↦ (wordIso F G e Z.as).hom) hunit htensor X
  | l_inv X =>
    exact (CommSq.horiz_inv (f := F.mapIso (λ_ X)) (i := G.mapIso (λ_ X))
      ⟨Functor.Monoidal.leftUnitor_hom_naturality_of_unit_tensor
        (e := fun Z ↦ (wordIso F G e Z.as).hom) hunit htensor X⟩).w
  | ρ_hom X =>
    exact Functor.Monoidal.rightUnitor_hom_naturality_of_unit_tensor
      (e := fun Z ↦ (wordIso F G e Z.as).hom) hunit htensor X
  | ρ_inv X =>
    exact (CommSq.horiz_inv (f := F.mapIso (ρ_ X)) (i := G.mapIso (ρ_ X))
      ⟨Functor.Monoidal.rightUnitor_hom_naturality_of_unit_tensor
        (e := fun Z ↦ (wordIso F G e Z.as).hom) hunit htensor X⟩).w
  | ε_right X => exact map_evaluation_rightDual_comp_wordIso_hom X
  | η_right X => exact map_coevaluation_rightDual_comp_wordIso_hom X
  | ε_left X => exact map_evaluation_leftDual_comp_wordIso_hom X
  | η_left X => exact map_coevaluation_leftDual_comp_wordIso_hom X
  | coupon g => exact he g
  | comp f g hf hg =>
    rw [Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc, hg, reassoc_of% hf]
  | whiskerLeft X f hf =>
    exact Functor.Monoidal.whiskerLeft_naturality_of_tensor
      (e := fun Z ↦ (wordIso F G e Z.as).hom) htensor X hf
  | whiskerRight f X hf =>
    exact Functor.Monoidal.whiskerRight_naturality_of_tensor
      (e := fun Z ↦ (wordIso F G e Z.as).hom) htensor X hf

/-- Two strong monoidal functors out of the free rigid monoidal category on `S` that agree up to
isomorphisms `e` on the generating objects, compatibly with every coupon, are isomorphic by a
monoidal natural isomorphism extending `e`. -/
def monoidalNatIso
    (he : ∀ g, F.map (coupon g) ≫ (wordIso F G e (S.tgt g)).hom =
      (wordIso F G e (S.src g)).hom ≫ G.map (coupon g)) :
    F ≅ G :=
  NatIso.ofComponents (fun X ↦ wordIso F G e X.as) fun f ↦ map_comp_wordIso_hom he f

variable (he : ∀ g, F.map (coupon g) ≫ (wordIso F G e (S.tgt g)).hom =
  (wordIso F G e (S.src g)).hom ≫ G.map (coupon g))

/-- The components of `monoidalNatIso he` are the isomorphisms `wordIso F G e`. -/
@[simp]
theorem monoidalNatIso_hom_app (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (monoidalNatIso he).hom.app X = (wordIso F G e X.as).hom := by rfl

/-- At a generating object, the component of `monoidalNatIso he` is the given isomorphism. -/
theorem monoidalNatIso_hom_app_of (a : S.Obj) :
    (monoidalNatIso he).hom.app (of a) = (e a).hom := by rfl

/-- The natural isomorphism `monoidalNatIso he` is monoidal. -/
instance isMonoidal_monoidalNatIso_hom : NatTrans.IsMonoidal (monoidalNatIso he).hom :=
  NatTrans.IsMonoidal.of_unit_tensor _ (wordIso_tensorUnit_hom F G e) (wordIso_tensor_hom F G e)

/-- A monoidal natural isomorphism between strong monoidal functors out of the free rigid monoidal
category is the `wordIso` of its components at the generating objects. -/
theorem wordIso_app {F G : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D} [F.Monoidal] [G.Monoidal] (α : F ≅ G)
    [NatTrans.IsMonoidal α.hom] (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    wordIso F G (fun a ↦ α.app (of a)) X = α.app ⟨X⟩ := by
  ext
  induction X with
  | of a => exact congrArg Iso.hom (wordIso_of F G _ a)
  | unit =>
    exact (wordIso_tensorUnit_hom F G _).trans
      (NatTrans.IsMonoidal.app_tensorUnit_eq_η_comp_ε α.hom).symm
  | tensor X Y hX hY =>
    refine (wordIso_tensor_hom F G _ ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩).trans ?_
    rw [hX, hY, Iso.app_hom, Iso.app_hom]
    exact (NatTrans.IsMonoidal.app_tensor_eq_δ_comp_tensor_comp_μ α.hom ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩).symm
  | rightDual X hX =>
    refine (wordIso_rightDual_hom F G _ ⟨X⟩).trans ?_
    -- The mate of `α⁻¹` at `X` is inverse to `α⁻¹` at `Xᘁ`, by monoidality of `α⁻¹`.
    have h := NatTrans.rightMate_app_comp_app α.inv ⟨X⟩ (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)ᘁ
    have hinv : (wordIso F G (fun a ↦ α.app (of a)) X).inv = α.inv.app ⟨X⟩ :=
      ((Iso.inv_eq_inv _ _).mpr hX).trans (Iso.app_inv α ⟨X⟩)
    rw [hinv, Iso.app_hom]
    exact (Iso.comp_inv_eq_id (α.app ⟨X⟩ᘁ)).mp h
  | leftDual X hX =>
    refine (wordIso_leftDual_hom F G _ ⟨X⟩).trans ?_
    -- The left mate of `α⁻¹` at `X` is inverse to `α⁻¹` at `ᘁX`, by monoidality of `α⁻¹`.
    have h := NatTrans.leftMate_app_comp_app α.inv (ᘁ(⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)) ⟨X⟩
    have hinv : (wordIso F G (fun a ↦ α.app (of a)) X).inv = α.inv.app ⟨X⟩ :=
      ((Iso.inv_eq_inv _ _).mpr hX).trans (Iso.app_inv α ⟨X⟩)
    rw [hinv, Iso.app_hom]
    exact (Iso.comp_inv_eq_id (α.app (ᘁ(⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)))).mp h

end Uniqueness

section WordIso

open Functor.LaxMonoidal Functor.OplaxMonoidal

variable {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] [MonoidalCategory D] [RigidCategory D]

/-- The comparison between the image of a formal rigid object under a strong monoidal functor `F`
out of the free rigid monoidal category and the evaluation of that object at the images of the
generating objects. It is built from the tensorators and unit comparison of `F`; at a dual it is
the comparison `F.mapRightDualIso` (or `F.mapLeftDualIso`) between the image of the chosen dual and
the chosen dual of the image, followed by the adjoint mate of the inverse comparison at the
object. -/
noncomputable def mapWordIso (F : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D) [F.Monoidal] :
    ∀ X : RigidObject S.Obj, F.obj ⟨X⟩ ≅ RigidObject.eval (fun a ↦ F.obj (of a)) X
  | .of _ => Iso.refl _
  | .unit => (Functor.Monoidal.εIso F).symm
  | .tensor X Y => (Functor.Monoidal.μIso F ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩).symm ≪≫ (mapWordIso F X ⊗ᵢ mapWordIso F Y)
  | .rightDual X => F.mapRightDualIso ⟨X⟩ ≪≫ (mapWordIso F X).symm.rightAdjointMate
  | .leftDual X => F.mapLeftDualIso ⟨X⟩ ≪≫ (mapWordIso F X).symm.leftAdjointMate

section Computation

variable (F : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D) [F.Monoidal]

@[simp]
theorem mapWordIso_of (a : S.Obj) : mapWordIso F (.of a) = Iso.refl (F.obj (of a)) :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem mapWordIso_unit_hom : (mapWordIso F .unit).hom = η F :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem mapWordIso_unit_inv : (mapWordIso F .unit).inv = ε F :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem mapWordIso_tensor_hom (X Y : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    (mapWordIso F (X.tensor Y)).hom =
      δ F ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩ ≫ ((mapWordIso F X).hom ⊗ₘ (mapWordIso F Y).hom) :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem mapWordIso_tensor_inv (X Y : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    (mapWordIso F (X.tensor Y)).inv =
      ((mapWordIso F X).inv ⊗ₘ (mapWordIso F Y).inv) ≫ μ F ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩ :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem mapWordIso_rightDual_hom (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    (mapWordIso F X.rightDual).hom =
      (F.mapRightDualIso (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)).hom ≫ ((mapWordIso F X).inv)ᘁ :=
  (Iso.trans_hom _ _).trans (congrArg (_ ≫ ·) (Iso.rightAdjointMate_hom _))

@[simp]
theorem mapWordIso_rightDual_inv (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    (mapWordIso F X.rightDual).inv =
      ((mapWordIso F X).hom)ᘁ ≫ (F.mapRightDualIso (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)).inv :=
  (Iso.trans_inv _ _).trans (congrArg (· ≫ _) (Iso.rightAdjointMate_inv _))

@[simp]
theorem mapWordIso_leftDual_hom (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    (mapWordIso F X.leftDual).hom =
      (F.mapLeftDualIso (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)).hom ≫ (ᘁ(mapWordIso F X).inv) :=
  (Iso.trans_hom _ _).trans (congrArg (_ ≫ ·) (Iso.leftAdjointMate_hom _))

@[simp]
theorem mapWordIso_leftDual_inv (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    (mapWordIso F X.leftDual).inv =
      (ᘁ(mapWordIso F X).hom) ≫ (F.mapLeftDualIso (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)).inv :=
  (Iso.trans_inv _ _).trans (congrArg (· ≫ _) (Iso.leftAdjointMate_inv _))

/-- At a right dual, the comparison `mapWordIso` is the mate of the inverse comparison at the
object, with respect to the image pairing of `F` and the chosen pairing of the evaluation. -/
theorem mapWordIso_rightDual_hom_eq_rightMate (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    (mapWordIso F X.rightDual).hom =
      ExactPairing.rightMate HasRightDual.exact (F.mapExactPairing ⟨X⟩ (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)ᘁ)
        (mapWordIso F X).inv := by
  simp only [mapWordIso_rightDual_hom, Functor.mapRightDualIso_hom_eq_rightMate,
    rightAdjointMate_eq_rightMate, ← ExactPairing.comp_rightMate, Category.comp_id]
  -- The two sides differ only in the implicit duals of the mate, `⟨X⟩ᘁ` against
  -- `⟨X.rightDual⟩`, which agree by definition of the duals of `S.FreeRigid`.
  rfl

/-- At a right dual, the inverse of `mapWordIso` is the mate of the comparison at the object. -/
theorem mapWordIso_rightDual_inv_eq_rightMate (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    (mapWordIso F X.rightDual).inv =
      ExactPairing.rightMate (F.mapExactPairing ⟨X⟩ (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)ᘁ) HasRightDual.exact
        (mapWordIso F X).hom := by
  simp only [mapWordIso_rightDual_inv, Functor.mapRightDualIso_inv_eq_rightMate,
    rightAdjointMate_eq_rightMate, ← ExactPairing.comp_rightMate, Category.id_comp]
  -- The two sides differ only in the implicit duals of the mate, `⟨X⟩ᘁ` against
  -- `⟨X.rightDual⟩`, which agree by definition of the duals of `S.FreeRigid`.
  rfl

/-- At a left dual, the comparison `mapWordIso` is the left mate of the inverse comparison at the
object, with respect to the image pairing of `F` and the chosen pairing of the evaluation. -/
theorem mapWordIso_leftDual_hom_eq_leftMate (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    (mapWordIso F X.leftDual).hom =
      ExactPairing.leftMate HasLeftDual.exact (F.mapExactPairing (ᘁ(⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)) ⟨X⟩)
        (mapWordIso F X).inv := by
  simp only [mapWordIso_leftDual_hom, Functor.mapLeftDualIso_hom_eq_leftMate,
    leftAdjointMate_eq_leftMate, ← ExactPairing.comp_leftMate, Category.comp_id]
  -- The two sides differ only in the implicit duals of the mate, `ᘁ⟨X⟩` against
  -- `⟨X.leftDual⟩`, which agree by definition of the duals of `S.FreeRigid`.
  rfl

/-- At a left dual, the inverse of `mapWordIso` is the left mate of the comparison at the
object. -/
theorem mapWordIso_leftDual_inv_eq_leftMate (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    (mapWordIso F X.leftDual).inv =
      ExactPairing.leftMate (F.mapExactPairing (ᘁ(⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)) ⟨X⟩) HasLeftDual.exact
        (mapWordIso F X).hom := by
  simp only [mapWordIso_leftDual_inv, Functor.mapLeftDualIso_inv_eq_leftMate,
    leftAdjointMate_eq_leftMate, ← ExactPairing.comp_leftMate, Category.id_comp]
  -- The two sides differ only in the implicit duals of the mate, `ᘁ⟨X⟩` against
  -- `⟨X.leftDual⟩`, which agree by definition of the duals of `S.FreeRigid`.
  rfl

end Computation

/-- For the strong monoidal functor `lift fo fc`, whose tensorators and unit comparison are
identities and which preserves chosen duals on the nose, the comparison `mapWordIso` is the
identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem mapWordIso_lift (fo : S.Obj → D)
    (fc : ∀ g : S.Coupon, RigidObject.eval fo (S.src g) ⟶ RigidObject.eval fo (S.tgt g))
    (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : mapWordIso (lift fo fc) X = Iso.refl (RigidObject.eval fo X) := by
  induction X with
  | of a => rfl
  | unit => rfl
  | tensor X Y hX hY =>
    ext
    refine (mapWordIso_tensor_hom (lift fo fc) X Y).trans ?_
    rw [hX, hY, Iso.refl_hom, Iso.refl_hom]
    -- The tensorator of `lift fo fc` is the identity (`lift_δ`), but its source and target are
    -- only definitionally equal to the tensor product of the evaluations, so `rw` cannot use it.
    exact (Category.id_comp _).trans (id_tensorHom_id _ _)
  | rightDual X hX =>
    ext
    refine (mapWordIso_rightDual_hom (lift fo fc) X).trans ?_
    rw [hX, lift_mapRightDualIso, Iso.refl_inv, Iso.refl_hom]
    -- The identities are typed at `(lift fo fc).obj ⟨X⟩ᘁ`, which is the right dual of
    -- `RigidObject.eval fo X` only after unfolding `lift`, so `rw` cannot use
    -- `rightAdjointMate_id`.
    exact (Category.id_comp _).trans rightAdjointMate_id
  | leftDual X hX =>
    ext
    refine (mapWordIso_leftDual_hom (lift fo fc) X).trans ?_
    rw [hX, lift_mapLeftDualIso, Iso.refl_inv, Iso.refl_hom]
    -- As in the right dual case, the identities are only definitionally typed at the left dual
    -- of `RigidObject.eval fo X`.
    exact (Category.id_comp _).trans leftAdjointMate_id

/- The inductive steps of `wordIso_eq_mapWordIso` at a right and at a left dual: both sides are
mates with respect to the image pairings of `F` and `G`, and the mate of the composite splits at
the chosen pairings of the two evaluations. -/

private theorem wordIso_rightDual_hom_eq_mapWordIso (F G : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D) [F.Monoidal]
    [G.Monoidal] (e : ∀ a, F.obj (of a) ≅ G.obj (of a)) (X : RigidObject S.Obj)
    (hX : wordIso F G e X = mapWordIso F X ≪≫ RigidObject.evalIso e X ≪≫ (mapWordIso G X).symm) :
    (wordIso F G e X.rightDual).hom = (mapWordIso F X.rightDual ≪≫
      RigidObject.evalIso e X.rightDual ≪≫ (mapWordIso G X.rightDual).symm).hom := by
  have hinv := congrArg Iso.inv hX
  rw [Iso.trans_inv, Iso.trans_inv, Iso.symm_inv] at hinv
  rw [Iso.trans_hom, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, mapWordIso_rightDual_hom_eq_rightMate,
    mapWordIso_rightDual_inv_eq_rightMate, RigidObject.evalIso_rightDual,
    Iso.rightAdjointMate_hom, Iso.symm_hom, rightAdjointMate_eq_rightMate]
  refine (wordIso_rightDual_hom F G e ⟨X⟩).trans ?_
  -- Both sides are mates with respect to the image pairings of `F` and `G`; split the mate of
  -- the composite at the chosen pairings of the two evaluations.
  rw [hinv, ExactPairing.comp_rightMate _
      (HasRightDual.exact (X := RigidObject.eval (fun a ↦ F.obj (of a)) X)),
    ExactPairing.comp_rightMate _
      (HasRightDual.exact (X := RigidObject.eval (fun a ↦ G.obj (of a)) X))]
  -- The two sides now agree up to the implicit duals of the mates, `⟨X⟩ᘁ` against
  -- `⟨X.rightDual⟩`, which agree by definition of the duals of `S.FreeRigid`.
  rfl

private theorem wordIso_leftDual_hom_eq_mapWordIso (F G : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D) [F.Monoidal]
    [G.Monoidal] (e : ∀ a, F.obj (of a) ≅ G.obj (of a)) (X : RigidObject S.Obj)
    (hX : wordIso F G e X = mapWordIso F X ≪≫ RigidObject.evalIso e X ≪≫ (mapWordIso G X).symm) :
    (wordIso F G e X.leftDual).hom = (mapWordIso F X.leftDual ≪≫
      RigidObject.evalIso e X.leftDual ≪≫ (mapWordIso G X.leftDual).symm).hom := by
  have hinv := congrArg Iso.inv hX
  rw [Iso.trans_inv, Iso.trans_inv, Iso.symm_inv] at hinv
  rw [Iso.trans_hom, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, mapWordIso_leftDual_hom_eq_leftMate,
    mapWordIso_leftDual_inv_eq_leftMate, RigidObject.evalIso_leftDual,
    Iso.leftAdjointMate_hom, Iso.symm_hom, leftAdjointMate_eq_leftMate]
  refine (wordIso_leftDual_hom F G e ⟨X⟩).trans ?_
  -- As in the right dual case, split the left mate of the composite at the chosen pairings.
  rw [hinv, ExactPairing.comp_leftMate _
      (HasLeftDual.exact (Y := RigidObject.eval (fun a ↦ F.obj (of a)) X)),
    ExactPairing.comp_leftMate _
      (HasLeftDual.exact (Y := RigidObject.eval (fun a ↦ G.obj (of a)) X))]
  -- As in the right dual case, the two sides agree up to the implicit left duals of the mates.
  rfl

/-- The isomorphisms `wordIso F G e` between two strong monoidal functors out of the free rigid
monoidal category are the comparisons `mapWordIso` composed with the extension
`RigidObject.evalIso e` of `e` to formal rigid objects. -/
theorem wordIso_eq_mapWordIso (F G : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D) [F.Monoidal] [G.Monoidal]
    (e : ∀ a, F.obj (of a) ≅ G.obj (of a)) (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    wordIso F G e X = mapWordIso F X ≪≫ RigidObject.evalIso e X ≪≫ (mapWordIso G X).symm := by
  induction X with
  | of a =>
    ext
    rw [Iso.trans_hom, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, mapWordIso_of, mapWordIso_of,
      RigidObject.evalIso_of, Iso.refl_hom, Iso.refl_inv]
    -- The identities are typed at `F.obj ⟨.of a⟩`, which is `F.obj (of a)` only after unfolding
    -- `of`, so `simp` cannot cancel them.
    exact (congrArg Iso.hom (wordIso_of F G e a)).trans
      ((Category.id_comp _).trans (Category.comp_id _)).symm
  | unit =>
    ext
    rw [Iso.trans_hom, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, mapWordIso_unit_hom, mapWordIso_unit_inv,
      RigidObject.evalIso_unit, Iso.refl_hom]
    -- The identity is typed at `RigidObject.eval _ .unit`, which is `𝟙_ D` only after unfolding
    -- `RigidObject.eval`, so `simp` cannot cancel it.
    exact (wordIso_tensorUnit_hom F G e).trans (congrArg (η F ≫ ·) (Category.id_comp _).symm)
  | tensor X Y hX hY =>
    ext
    have hX' := congrArg Iso.hom hX
    have hY' := congrArg Iso.hom hY
    rw [Iso.trans_hom, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom] at hX' hY' ⊢
    rw [mapWordIso_tensor_hom, mapWordIso_tensor_inv, RigidObject.evalIso_tensor, tensorIso_hom]
    refine (wordIso_tensor_hom F G e ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩).trans ?_
    -- The tensor products on the right meet at `RigidObject.eval _ (X.tensor Y)`, which is a
    -- tensor product only after unfolding `RigidObject.eval`, so `simp` cannot merge them; the
    -- tensors of composites on the left are split instead.
    rw [hX', hY', ← MonoidalCategory.tensorHom_comp_tensorHom,
      ← MonoidalCategory.tensorHom_comp_tensorHom]
    conv_lhs => simp only [Category.assoc]
    exact (Category.assoc (δ F ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩) _ _).symm
  | rightDual X hX =>
    ext
    exact wordIso_rightDual_hom_eq_mapWordIso F G e X hX
  | leftDual X hX =>
    ext
    exact wordIso_leftDual_hom_eq_mapWordIso F G e X hX

/-- From a lift to a strong monoidal functor `G`, `wordIso` is the extension of the isomorphisms of
generators to formal rigid objects followed by the inverse of the comparison `mapWordIso G`. -/
theorem wordIso_lift_left {fo : S.Obj → D}
    (fc : ∀ g : S.Coupon, RigidObject.eval fo (S.src g) ⟶ RigidObject.eval fo (S.tgt g))
    (G : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D) [G.Monoidal] (e : ∀ a, fo a ≅ G.obj (of a))
    (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    wordIso (lift fo fc) G e X = RigidObject.evalIso e X ≪≫ (mapWordIso G X).symm := by
  refine (wordIso_eq_mapWordIso (lift fo fc) G e X).trans ?_
  rw [mapWordIso_lift]
  -- The identity is typed at `RigidObject.eval fo X`, which is the source of `evalIso e X` only
  -- after unfolding `lift`, so `rw` cannot use `Iso.refl_trans`.
  exact Iso.refl_trans _

/-- Between two lifts, `wordIso` is the extension of the isomorphisms of generators to formal rigid
objects. -/
@[simp]
theorem wordIso_lift_lift {fo fo' : S.Obj → D}
    (fc : ∀ g : S.Coupon, RigidObject.eval fo (S.src g) ⟶ RigidObject.eval fo (S.tgt g))
    (fc' : ∀ g : S.Coupon, RigidObject.eval fo' (S.src g) ⟶ RigidObject.eval fo' (S.tgt g))
    (e : ∀ a, fo a ≅ fo' a) (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    wordIso (lift fo fc) (lift fo' fc') e X = RigidObject.evalIso e X := by
  refine (wordIso_lift_left fc (lift fo' fc') e X).trans ?_
  rw [mapWordIso_lift]
  -- As in `wordIso_lift_left`, the identity is only definitionally typed at the target of
  -- `evalIso e X`.
  exact (congrArg (RigidObject.evalIso e X ≪≫ ·) (Iso.refl_symm _)).trans (Iso.trans_refl _)

/-- From the lift of the generator images of `F` to `F`, `wordIso` of the identities is the
inverse of the comparison `mapWordIso F`. -/
theorem wordIso_lift_refl (F : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D) [F.Monoidal]
    (fc : ∀ g : S.Coupon, RigidObject.eval (fun a ↦ F.obj (of a)) (S.src g) ⟶
      RigidObject.eval (fun a ↦ F.obj (of a)) (S.tgt g)) (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    wordIso (lift (fun a ↦ F.obj (of a)) fc) F (fun a ↦ Iso.refl (F.obj (of a))) X =
      (mapWordIso F X).symm := by
  refine (wordIso_lift_left fc F _ X).trans ?_
  rw [RigidObject.evalIso_refl]
  exact Iso.refl_trans _

/-- The extension to formal rigid objects of the components of a monoidal natural isomorphism at
the generating objects is its component at the object, conjugated by the comparisons
`mapWordIso`. -/
theorem evalIso_app {F G : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D} [F.Monoidal] [G.Monoidal] (α : F ≅ G)
    [NatTrans.IsMonoidal α.hom] (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    RigidObject.evalIso (fun a ↦ α.app (of a)) X =
      (mapWordIso F X).symm ≪≫ α.app ⟨X⟩ ≪≫ mapWordIso G X := by
  rw [← wordIso_app α X, wordIso_eq_mapWordIso]
  ext
  simp

end WordIso

